<!--Engine Documentation — RenderEngineContract
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender.documentation.RenderEngineContract-->
<edoc:RenderEngineContract xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:edoc="org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    RenderEngine methods this package implements
  </is>
  <documentation>
    BOM Core defines the interface. This package implements it. Method set:

        interface RenderEngine {
          compile(block, processor, context): RenderOutput
          renderTemplate(block, templatePath): RenderOutput
          renderTemplates(block, templatePaths): RenderOutput
          copyTemplate(sourcePath, targetPath): RenderOutput
          callLLM(block, prompt, context): RenderOutput
        }

    compile — deterministic transformation. The processor supplies the algorithm
    as processor.compile(block, context). The engine calls that method with the
    given RenderContext and returns its RenderOutput unchanged. It does not read
    file content. The MachineBlocks SCAD processors use this method. If the
    processor has no compile method, compile returns files: [] and diagnostic
    BML_ENGINE_COMPILE_CALLBACK_MISSING.

    renderTemplate — load one template and substitute variables from the block.
    renderTemplates — the same for several template paths (one processor, several
    output files). Example shape: a processor for a device that emits a script
    template and a config template.

    copyTemplate — copy a file from sourcePath to targetPath with no rewrite.
    Used when a service file is already the desired artifact.

    callLLM — reserved. This package does not call a model.

    This implementation slice runs compile. renderTemplate, renderTemplates,
    copyTemplate, and callLLM return files: [] and diagnostic
    BML_ENGINE_STRATEGY_UNSUPPORTED. Template substitution and file copy without
    a Node-only API are not specified yet. callLLM stays deferred.

    This package does not call registerTarget.

    The engine does not choose the method. The BlockProcessor does, inside
    process(block, engine, context). The block is a BlockDefinition or a
    BlockInstance. The engine does not inspect it. A processor that only
    delegates should not be given an engine call at all; its target lists
    delegates and may leave engine unset.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="edoc:Strategies" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</edoc:RenderEngineContract>
